@startuml machine-states
!include _style.puml

' States of a machine. The health indicator is an attribute of the machine,
' not a state: it falls in steps of 0.125 while the machine is operational.

[*] --> Operational : health = 1

state Operational {
  [*] --> Starved
  Starved --> Processing : part available
  Processing --> Blocked : cycle complete,\ndownstream buffer full
  Processing --> Starved : cycle complete,\npart passed on,\nno part waiting
  Processing --> Processing : cycle complete,\npart passed on,\nnext part waiting
  Blocked --> Starved : space downstream,\nno part waiting
  Blocked --> Processing : space downstream,\nnext part waiting
}

Operational --> Operational : degradation event\n[health > 0.125]\n/ health = health - 0.125
Operational --> Operational : alarm\n/ create work order

note on link
  Only a part in process is scrapped. A machine that is blocked hands over its
  finished part first, and a starved machine has taken none (A9).
end note
Operational --> AwaitingRepair : degradation event\n[health = 0.125]\n/ health = 0,\nscrap part in process,\ncreate work order
AwaitingRepair --> CorrectiveRepair : maintainer available
CorrectiveRepair --> Operational : after 20 hours\n/ health = 1

Operational --> PreventiveRepair : maintainer arrives\n[work order pending]\n/ pause processing
PreventiveRepair --> Operational : after 2.5 hours [health >= 0.5]\nor 5 hours [health < 0.5]\n/ health = 1, resume

note right of PreventiveRepair
  The part in process is paused and keeps its remaining cycle time (A11).
  A machine has at most one open work order (A12). The model records
  CorrectiveRepair and PreventiveRepair as the one state under_repair and
  tells them apart by the RepairKind of the repair.
end note
@enduml
